{
  "id": "magnitude-effect",
  "term": "magnitude effect",
  "definition": "The magnitude effect is a time-perception phenomenon in which a stimulus that is greater on some non-time feature, such as size, pitch, brightness, or numerical value, is experienced as lasting longer than a smaller or weaker stimulus even when both last the same objective time. In other words, differences in magnitude can distort perceived duration.",
